     (description . "Link the exact CML-generated M1 object and M2 runtime into the M3 image, boot in QEMU, and emit WSM-OS RESULT schema=1 value=(A . B) status=ok. Commit source fixture, oracle output, contract SHAs, generated-artifact digest and serial transcript together. Compare canonical value and failure class, not only exit status. Mark QEMU-BOOT-PARITY, never physical-hardware parity.")))

   ("WSM-OS-M4-COMPILER-ARTIFACT-BUNDLE" .
    ((priority . 9.5)
     (done . t)
     (capabilities . (cml compiler x86_64 assembly reproducibility testing proof))
     (depends-on . (WSM-OS-CML-X86-FREESTANDING-M1 WSM-OS-HOST-RUNTIME-PARITY-M2))
     (origin . wsm-os)
     (description . "Prepare the compiler-owned half of M4 without touching boot/runtime: one deterministic command must compile the frozen WSM fixture through pinned CML into GNU assembly and an object, then emit a manifest containing source digest, CML SHA, target-contract SHA, object digest, exported entry symbol and exact undefined wsm_* imports. Run twice and require byte-identical assembly/object/manifest; fail closed on any extra import. Commit the small fixture bundle or a reproducible generator as decided by existing artifact policy. Do not add language features or claim QEMU parity.")))

   ("WSM-OS-CML-X86-FIXNUM-BRANCH-M5A" .
    ((priority . 7.5)
     (capabilities . (cml compiler x86_64 assembly conformance testing proof))
     (depends-on . (WSM-OS-FIRST-QEMU-PARITY-M4))
     (origin . wsm-os)
     (description . "Extend the x86_64 freestanding backend by exactly one conformance slice: ABI-range fixnum literals, atomic eq, and cond branching on canonical NIL only. Add target preflight, host-link parity and QEMU parity fixtures against the pinned my-lisp oracle. Unsupported arithmetic and closures must remain named compile errors; no silent fallback.")))

   ("WSM-OS-CML-X86-ARITHMETIC-M5B" .
    ((priority . 7.0)
     (capabilities . (cml compiler x86_64 assembly arithmetic conformance testing proof))
     (depends-on . (WSM-OS-CML-X86-FIXNUM-BRANCH-M5A))
     (origin . wsm-os)
     (description . "Add the next isolated x86_64 conformance slice: checked fixnum addition and subtraction with exact overflow mapped to the ratified runtime error boundary. Differentially verify boundary values against pinned my-lisp in hosted and QEMU paths. Do not add multiplication, closures, GC, or widen the numeric model in the same change.")))

   ("WSM-OS-CONFORMANCE-LADDER-M5" .
    ((priority . 7.0)
     (capabilities . (my-lisp cml x86_64 assembly conformance testing proof))
     (depends-on . (WSM-OS-FIRST-QEMU-PARITY-M4))
     (origin . wsm-os)
     (description . "Expand conformance one obligation at a time: () truth/branch; fixnum and symbol identity; car/cdr/cons; nested canonical printing; named type/arity/OOM errors; one closure only after environment layout is ratified. Every fixture must match pinned my-lisp through CML admission, hosted runtime and QEMU. Do not broaden to keyboard/disk/network/GUI.")))

   ("WSM-OS-MYLISP-NOSTD-DECISION-M6" .
    ((priority . 6.0)
     (capabilities . (rust no-std my-lisp architecture testing evidence))
     (depends-on . (WSM-OS-FIRST-QEMU-PARITY-M4))
     (origin . wsm-os)
     (description . "After the AOT witness is green, run a bounded portability spike for my-lisp core: classify std imports, move eligible containers to alloc/core behind features, make time/stdin/global capability registry explicit platform services, and test no_std+alloc compilation separately. Decide with measured code size/complexity whether to retain AOT only or add an interactive interpreter. Do not rewrite the hosted core or claim Rc collects cycles.")))

   ("WSM-OS-COPYING-GC-M7" .
    ((priority . 5.0)
     (capabilities . (rust memory x86_64 garbage-collection architecture))
     (depends-on . (WSM-OS-CONFORMANCE-LADDER-M5))
     (origin . wsm-os)
     (description . "Replace the initial bounded bump allocator with a semi-space copying collector. Leverage the fact that all cons cells are 16-bytes and tags perfectly distinguish pointers. Implement from-space/to-space swapping, root tracing from the WsmContext, and graph traversal. Do not implement generational or ephemeral GC. Maintain explicit OOM when both spaces are full.")))

   ("WSM-OS-STACK-BUFFER-M8" .
    ((priority . 5.0)
     (capabilities . (rust memory architecture runtime))
     (depends-on . (WSM-OS-HOST-RUNTIME-PARITY-M2))
     (origin . wsm-os)
     (description . "Implement the WSM call stack as a contiguous array of Word in the WsmContext (stack_start, stack_ptr, stack_end). Use this for execution frames instead of heap-allocating every frame. Keep it strictly as the third storage primitive alongside registers and the cons heap.")))

   ("WSM-OS-TINY-ISA-M9" .
    ((priority . 4.0)
     (capabilities . (cml compiler architecture interpreter))
     (depends-on . (WSM-OS-MYLISP-NOSTD-DECISION-M6))
     (origin . wsm-os)
     (description . "Design a tiny ~15-instruction WSM bytecode ISA (LOAD_CONST, LOAD_SYMBOL, CONS, CAR, CALL, BRANCH_FALSE, etc.). Add a second backend path to CML to emit this bytecode, and implement a tiny tag-dispatch interpreter in wsm-os. This provides a portable alternative to x86_64 AOT emission and sets the stage for fpga-lisp.")))

   ("WSM-OS-LIVE-IMAGE-M10" .
    ((priority . 3.0)
     (capabilities . (architecture repl operating-system runtime))
     (depends-on . (WSM-OS-CONFORMANCE-LADDER-M5))
     (origin . wsm-os)
     (description . "Evolve the system from a single AOT frozen expression toward a live Lisp environment. Implement a symbol/function binding table (where name identity remains separated from the symbol ID). Allow replacing function bindings at runtime and evaluating multiple forms sequentially, laying the groundwork for a persistent image."))))))
